##### Contributions.

In summary, this paper provides:

* • a complete hypothesis-class characterization of realizable strong universal Bayes-consistency for general metric losses, via the infinite unbounded-gap Littlestone tree obstruction (Theorem [4.5](https://arxiv.org/html/2605.03823v2#S4.Thmtheorem5 "Theorem 4.5 (Main characterization). ‣ 4 Main result: characterization of ℋ ‣ Realizable Bayes-Consistency for General Metric Losses")); * • a constructive learning rule in the obstruction-free regime, proven to be strongly universally Bayes-consistent in the realizable setting (Theorem [6.5](https://arxiv.org/html/2605.03823v2#S6.Thmtheorem5 "Theorem 6.5 (Realizable upper bound). ‣ 6.6 Realizable strong universal Bayes-consistency ‣ 6 Upper bound: absence of an infinite tree implies strong universal consistency ‣ Realizable Bayes-Consistency for General Metric Losses")); * • a separation demonstrating that natural finiteness-type conditions (e.g. candidates based on R⋆<∞R^{\star}<\infty) do not capture the correct characterization in the unbounded metric-loss realizable setting, resolving the realizable case of the open problem posed by Tsir Cohen & Kontorovich ([2022](https://arxiv.org/html/2605.03823v2#bib.bib10)).

