## 4 Main result: characterization of ℋ{\mathcal{H}}

ℋ{\mathcal{H}}

We now state the main theorem, which characterizes when strong universal Bayes-consistency is achievable in the realizable setting under general (possibly unbounded) metric losses. The characterization is in terms of a single combinatorial obstruction: an *unbounded-gap* Littlestone tree.

