## 6 Upper bound: absence of an infinite tree implies strong universal consistency

In this section we complete the argument that, under a suitable combinatorial condition on ℋ{\mathcal{H}}, strong universal Bayes-consistent learning is possible in the realizable case, even when the loss is unbounded.

